default-icons/melee.svg","name":"Tail","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"value":["finesse"],"otherTags":[]},"damageRolls":{"VTFjMAB5rExE92TP":{"damage":"1d6+2","damageType":"bludgeoning","category":null}},"bonus":{"value":9},"attackEffects":{"value":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}}},"effects":[],"_id":"nJJ23bXhbWHu7Egh","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"5.0.2","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1687476946842,"modifiedTime":1687477013542,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","name":"Illusory Attack","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>The false tarrasque creates a colossal illusory attack, which can appear as any damage type. In its normal form, Illusory Attack affects a @Template[type:cone|distance:10], but while Titanic Transformation is active, Illusory Attack can affect a @Template[type:cone|distance:30], a @Template[type:line|distance:60], or a @Template[type:burst|distance:10] with a range of 90 feet. Regardless of the area affected or the damage type it mimics, Illusory Attack deals @Damage[1d8[mental]] damage (@Check[type:will|dc:14|basic:true] save). A creature that critically succeeds, or a creature with a resistance, immunity, or vulnerability that should apply to the apparent damage type, recognizes that the Illusory Attack is actually an illusion. Such a creature gains a +2 circumstance bonus to saving throws against Illusory Attack.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["illusion","mental","primal"]},